# Docker

The official image runs three processes behind one port: the Rust server, the Node UI server, and nginx in front of both. nginx sends API paths (`/v1`, `/auth`, `/platform`, `/mcp`, `/openapi.json`, `/healthz`, `/readyz`) to Rust unchanged and everything else to the UI. It also serves public gRPC on port 50051. Clients derive the gRPC address from the server URL (same host, port 50051), so publish both ports on the same host.

No Wyrd image is published yet. Build the official image from the commit you are running and use its immutable image ID:

```bash
mise run docker:build                              # tags the local image `wyrd`
IMAGE="$(docker image inspect -f '{{.Id}}' wyrd)"  # sha256:… — record it with the commit
```

Once a release is published, use its published digest instead.

The container keeps no database. Local artifact storage and Bifrost data live under `/var/lib/wyrd`; mount a volume there, or point storage at a bucket.

## First run

```bash
# The tenant and platform logins you created (see Database).
DB_URLS=(-e WYRD_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://wyrd_tenant:…@db:5432/wyrd"
         -e WYRD_PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://wyrd_platform:…@db:5432/wyrd")

# 1. Once per release, migrate. It connects as the platform login.
docker run --rm "${DB_URLS[@]}" "$IMAGE" wyrd-server migrate

# 2. Serve.
docker run -d --name wyrd -p 8080:8080 -p 50051:50051 \
  -e APP_ENV=production "${DB_URLS[@]}" \
  -e WYRD_STORAGE_URL=file:///var/lib/wyrd/storage \
  -e WYRD_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/signing.pem \
  -v wyrd-data:/var/lib/wyrd -v "$PWD/signing.pem:/run/secrets/signing.pem:ro" \
  "$IMAGE"

# 3. Create the first tenant. Safe to re-run: an existing tenant is a no-op.
docker exec wyrd wyrd-server setup --tenant acme
```

`setup` initializes the platform root if needed, then creates the tenant through the running server. It prints the tenant's administrative credential once. If the root was already initialized, export its credential as `WYRD_PLATFORM_CREDENTIAL` first. If the schema is not migrated or does not match the binary, the server refuses to start with `WYRD_SQL_503_SCHEMA_NOT_READY`; run step 1 and start again.

